  "caption": "Near-positive enrichment under AB-blocked validation.",
  "reading_guide": "Read the curves at the same per-fold budget k; hits sum the five folds and EF gives each fold equal weight. The dotted vertical line is k=20, corresponding to 100 selections overall. H-soft gives 68 hits and EF=62.1024, compared with 10, 1 and 0 hits for additive Ridge, mean and the fixed random realization. The event is V<=2. Endpoint labels refer to k=100; the separate zoom window enlarges the marked low-EF band of the parent panel, with matching log-budget coordinates and connector lines. The dashed horizontal line is EF=1, the uniform-random expectation, not the realized random curve. Per-fold N/M/h and existing unadjusted hypergeometric p values remain in F2_fold_uniform_null.csv; they are descriptive references after development selection, not a pooled test.",
